repository-code: "https://github.com/k-roy/RECTIFY"
url: "https://rectify-rna.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  RECTIFY is a unified framework for correcting 5' and 3' end mapping
  artifacts in poly(A)-tailed RNA sequencing data, with support for
  Nanopore direct RNA-seq, QuantSeq REV, ONT PCR-cDNA, NET-seq, and any
  oligo-dT-primed RNA-seq. It combines multi-aligner consensus
  (minimap2, mapPacBio, gapmm2, uLTRA, deSALT) with poly(A) walk-back,
  indel correction, 5'-splice-junction rescue, false-junction handling
  for poly(A) tails landing on genomic A-tracts, and optional NET-seq
  NNLS deconvolution. Downstream analyses include adaptive
  valley-based CPA clustering and DESeq2 at both gene and
  cluster resolution.
keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - polyadenylation
  - cleavage and polyadenylation
  - direct RNA sequencing
  - nanopore
  - Oxford Nanopore Technologies
  - QuantSeq
  - NET-seq
  - 3' end mapping
  - splice junction
  - multi-aligner consensus
